# WS2-08. # Sources: spec/06-functions.md G-6 (monomorphized instances) and spec/03 §3/§5: a generic instance moves and drops exactly like the concrete code; an i32 instance copies.
 Wrap<i32> is duplicable (copy); Wrap<Tok> is move-only and drops its field once.
profiles: host
with: tok.clo
expect: output
contrast: v: 5, n: 2 ==> v: 6, n: 2
contrast-expect: output
--- output
use 1
5 5
end
drop 1
--- contrast-output
use 1
6 6
end
drop 1
